A||||4||Ironhorse||I ask too many question don't I :)||||1||
Z||000000||Ironhorse||04-27-2000||01:23 AM||||Will a 86 - 88 Fiero Gt taillight fit on 85 GT?  if yes or no, explain how they are different.. if it will work is it plug n play or is modification require?   Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ozzy||04-27-2000||01:39 AM||||Nada dude. The 85 GT is a notchback style. 86 1/2 - 88 are fastback style. Tail lights are complete different design to suit the fastback decklid  and rear clip. SOme folks here have converted the notchback to a fastback. Requires fastback clip, decklid, tail lights and illuminated "PONTIAC" emblem. <P>The early half of the 86 GT is a notchback I believe.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||04-27-2000||02:59 AM||||Actually if it is an 86 GT it is a fastback. Only 85GTs were notchbacks.<P>My 88 Coupe has GT taillights in it. It was simple to do. All I had to do is change the rear clip, decklid and rear wiring harness  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||04-27-2000||03:25 AM||||The lighted "pontiac" callout is part of the tailights.  The clip and tail lights are pretty expensive, if you manage to find some in good shape.  especially the tail lights. mucho money.<BR>notchback  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nback_lights.jpg">  <BR>Fastback  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fback_lights.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 04-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ozzy||04-27-2000||09:55 PM||||Oh Man!! See, there I go stepping up to the "Fiero Expert" podium and...I blew it! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Listen to these guys Ironhorse. SCCA and Standard are right. I was thinking about the 85 GT and 86 SE being the same. (Is that a good enough excuse?? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) SCCA especially. He did the fastback conversion on his Coupe.<P><BR>Mistaken Ozzy<P>||||reg||11
